<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
        <worksheet xml:id="sec_practical_sine" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
                <title>Practical Applications of Sine and Cosine</title>
                <introduction>
                        <example>
                                <statement>
                                        <p>
                                                We will show how to use sine, cosine, and similar triangles to solve a practical problem.
                                        </p>
                                        <figure xml:id='fig_river1'>
                                                <caption>Two Gatehouses on a Canal Lock</caption>
                                                <image width='60%'>
                                                        <description><p>An image showing a canal lock with a gatehouse on each side.</p></description>
                                                        <latex-image>
                                                                \begin{tikzpicture}
                                                                \coordinate (O) at (-3,0);
                                                                \coordinate (T0) at (0,0);
                                                                \coordinate (T1) at (0,2.5);
                                                                \draw
                                                                ($(O)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(O)-(0,0.3)$)
                                                                ($(T0)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(T0)-(0,0.3)$)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[stealth-stealth]
                                                                ($(O)-(0,0.2)$) -- node[midway,below] {\(30\)m} ($(T0)-(0,0.2)$)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[thick] (-3.5, 0) -- (1,0)
                                                                      (-3.5,2.5) -- (1,2.5)
                                                                ;
                                                                \fill
                                                                (-0.1,-0.05) rectangle (0.1,0.05)
                                                                (-0.1,2.45) rectangle (0.1,2.55)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[dashed] (O) -- (T1)
                                                                -- (T0);
                                                                \draw (-2.5,0)
                                                                arc[start angle=0, end angle=39.8, radius=0.5]
                                                                node[midway,right] {\scriptsize\(\theta\approx 0.69474\) rad}
                                                                ;
                                                                \end{tikzpicture}
                                                        </latex-image>
                                                </image>
                                        </figure>
                                        <p>
                                                        Amir is standing at the edge of a canal lock. There are gatehouses on each side of the lock. The gatehouse on the same side as Amir is located <m>30</m>m from them. Amir wants to find out how wide the lock is by finding how far one gatehouse is from the other. Amir measures the angle from the near gatehouse to the far gatehouse and finds that it is <m>0.69474\text{ rad}</m>.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                        How wide is the lock?
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                        We start by drawing a copy of the unit circle centered on Amir's position, and we will assign the distance between the two gatehouses to the variable <m>d</m>. Then, by dropping a perpendicular from the point, <m>P</m>, where the line from Amir to the far gatehouse crosses the circle, we have similar triangles.
                                                </p>
                                        <figure xml:id='fig_river2'>
                                                <caption>Canal Lock with Unit Circle</caption>
                                                <image width='60%'>
                                                        <description><p>Canal Lock with Unit Circle</p></description>
                                                        <latex-image>
                                                                \begin{tikzpicture}
                                                                \coordinate (O) at (-3,0);
                                                                \coordinate (T0) at (0,0);
                                                                \coordinate (T1) at (0,2.5);
                                                                \draw
                                                                ($(O)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(O)-(0,0.3)$)
                                                                ($(T0)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(T0)-(0,0.3)$)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[stealth-stealth]
                                                                ($(O)-(0,0.2)$) -- node[midway,below] {\(30\)m} ($(T0)-(0,0.2)$)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[thick] (-3.5, 0) -- (1,0)
                                                                      (-3.5,2.5) -- (1,2.5)
                                                                ;
                                                                \fill
                                                                (-0.1,-0.05) rectangle (0.1,0.05)
                                                                (-0.1,2.45) rectangle (0.1,2.55)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[dotted,thick] (O) -- (T1)
                                                                -- node[midway,right] {\(d\)} (T0);
                                                                \draw (-2.5,0)
                                                                arc[start angle=0, end angle=39.8, radius=0.5]
%                                                                node[midway,right] {\scriptsize\(\theta\approx 0.69474\) rad}
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw (O) circle (1) ;
                                                                \draw[dashed] 
                                                                ($(O) - (0,1.1)$) -- ($(O)+(0,1.1)$)
                                                                ($(O) - (1.1,0)$) -- (O)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[dotted,thick] let \p1 = ($(39.8:1)-(3,0)$) in
                                                                (\p1) node[right] {\scriptsize\(P\)} -- (\x1,0)
                                                                ;
                                                                \end{tikzpicture}
                                                        </latex-image>
                                                </image>
                                        </figure>
                                        <p>
                                                We know that <m>P</m> has coordinates <m>(\cos(0.69474),\sin(0.69474))</m> (which we will leave unevaluated until the end).  Furthermore, we know from similar triangles that corresponding parts are proportional, so we have
                                                <md>\frac{d}{\sin(0.69474)}=\frac{30\text{m}}{\cos(0.69474)}.</md>
                                        </p>
                                        <p>
                                                Multiplying both sides by <m>\sin(0.69474)</m>, we have
                                                <md>
                                                        <mrow>d&amp;=\frac{30\text{m}\sin(0.69474)}{\cos(0.69474)}</mrow>
                                                        <mrow>&amp;\approx 25\text{m} </mrow>
                                                </md>
                                        </p>
                                </statement>
                        </example>
                </introduction>
                <page>
                        <exercise xml:id='exer_tree_height'>
                                        <statement>
                                                <p>
                                                        Inaya wants to use trigonometry to measure the height of a tree. She walks <m>10</m>m away from the base of the tree and measures the angle to the top of the tree as shown in <xref ref='fig_tree'/>.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                                To the nearest tenth of a meter, how tall is the tree? That is, what is the value of <m>d</m> in meters?
                                                </p>
                                        <figure xml:id='fig_tree'>
                                                <caption>An Observer and a Tree</caption>
                                                <image width='60%'>
                                                        <description><p>Image of a tree and an observer 10m away.</p></description>
                                                        <latex-image>
                                                                \begin{tikzpicture}
                                                                % Observer
                                                                \coordinate (O) at (-2,0);
                                                                \node[above left] at (O) {Inaya};
                                                                \fill (O) circle (0.05);
                                                                % Tree Base
                                                                \coordinate (T0) at (0,0);
                                                                % Tree Top
                                                                \coordinate (T1) at (0,4.5);
                                                                % Tick marks for Observer and Tree Base
                                                                \draw
                                                                ($(O)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(O)-(0,0.3)$)
                                                                ($(T0)-(0,0.1)$) -- ($(T0)-(0,0.3)$)
                                                                ;
                                                                % Ground
                                                                \draw[thick]
                                                                        ($(O)+(-1,0)$) -- ($(T0)+(1,0)$);
                                                                ;
                                                                % Distance Arrow Between Observer and Base
                                                                \draw[stealth-stealth]
                                                                ($(O)-(0,0.2)$) -- node[midway,below] {\(10\)m} ($(T0)-(0,0.2)$)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[dotted,thick]
                                                                % Observer to tree top
                                                                        (O) -- (T1)
                                                                % base to tree top, labeled \(d\) midway
                                                                        -- node[midway,right] {\(d\)} (T0);
                                                                % Angle indicator
                                                                \draw[-stealth]
                                                                let
                                                                \p1 =  (O),
                                                                \p2 = (T0),
                                                                \p3 = (T1),
                                                                \n1 = {atan((\y3-\y2)/(\x2-\x1))},
                                                                \n2 = {\n1*3.14159/(180pt)},
                                                                in
                                                                ($(\p1)+(0.5,0)$)
                                                                arc[
                                                                        start angle=0,
                                                                        end angle=\n1,
                                                                        radius=0.5
                                                                ]
                                                                node[midway,right] {\scriptsize\(\theta\approx \pgfmathparse{\n2}\pgfmathresult\) rad}
                                                                ;
                                                                \end{tikzpicture}
                                                        </latex-image>
                                                </image>
                                        </figure>
                                        </statement>
                                        <answer>
                                                <p>
                                                                The tree is approximately <m>22.5</m>m tall.
                                                </p>
                                        </answer>
                                        <solution>
                                                <p>
                                                        Draw a circle that represents the unit circle around the point representing Inaya and set your coordinate axes so that this is the origin.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                                Drop a perpendicular from where the circle intersects the line from Inaya to the top of the tree. We then have a small triangle with corners at the origin, on the unit circle, and on the <m>x</m>-axis. This triangle is similar to the triangle from the origin to the top of the tree to the <m>x</m>-axis because the share the angle <m>\theta</m> and they both have right angles on the <m>x</m>-axis.
                                                </p>
                                                <p>
                                                        We know the coordinates of the point on the unit circle are <m>(\cos(\theta),\sin(theta))</m>, and we know that the sides of the small triangle are proportional to the sides of the big triangle. Thus, <m>\frac{d}{10\text{m}}=\frac{\sin(\theta)}{\cos(\theta)}</m>, so we have
                                                        <md>
                                                                <mrow>d&amp;=10\text{m}\frac{\sin(\theta)}{\cos(\theta)}</mrow>
                                                                <mrow> &amp;=10\text{m}\frac{\sin(1.15251)}{\cos(1.15251)}</mrow>
                                                                <mrow> &amp;=22.5\text{m}</mrow>
                                                        </md>
                                                </p>
                                        </solution>
                        </exercise>
                </page>
                <page>
                        <exercise xml:id='exer_train_dist'>
                                <statement>
                                        <p>
                                                        Micah is watching a train as it approaches. He is <m>10</m>m from the closest point on the track.
                                        </p>
                                        <p>
                                                <!-- Marker -->                                                        He observes that the train makes an angle of approximately <m>0.98273</m> radians, and then one second later an angle of approximately <m>0.89594</m> radians. How fast is the train travelling?
                                        </p>
                                        <figure xml:id='fig_train_position'>
                                                <caption>A Train on a Track</caption>
                                                <image width='60%'>
                                                        <description><p>Image of a train on a horizontal track with an observer vertically 10m below the track.</p></description>
                                                        <latex-image>
                                                                \begin{tikzpicture}
                                                                % Observer
                                                                \coordinate (O) at (0,0);
                                                                \node[below] at (O) {Micah};
                                                                \fill (O) circle (0.05);
                                                                % train position 1
                                                                \coordinate (T1) at (-3.0,2.0);
                                                                % train position 2
                                                                \coordinate (T2) at (-2.5,2.0);
                                                                % near point on tracks
                                                                \coordinate (N) at (0,2.0);
                                                                % train tracks
                                                                \draw[thick]
                                                                        ($(T1)+(-.5,0)$) -- ($(N)+(.5,0)$);
                                                                ;
                                                                % Distance Arrow Between Observer and near point of tracks
                                                                \draw[stealth-stealth]
                                                                (O) -- node[near end,right] {\(10\)m} (N)
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[dotted,thick]
                                                                % train 1 to observer to train 2
                                                                        (T1) -- (O) -- (T2)
                                                                ;
                                                                % Angle indicator
                                                                \draw[-stealth]
                                                                let
                                                                \p1 =  (O),
                                                                \p2 = (T1),
                                                                \p3 = (T2),
                                                                \p4 = (N),
                                                                \n1 = {atan(-(\x2-\x1)/(\y2-\y1))},
                                                                \n2 = {\n1*3.14159/(180pt)},
                                                                \n3 = {atan(-(\x3-\x1)/(\y3-\y1))},
                                                                \n4 = {\n3*3.14159/(180pt)},
                                                                \n5 = {0.2*(\y4-\y1)},
                                                                \n6 = {0.3*(\y4-\y1)},
                                                                in
                                                                ($(\p1)!0.2!(\p4)$)
                                                                arc[
                                                                        start angle=90,
                                                                        delta angle=\n1,
                                                                %radius=0.2
                                                                radius={\n5},
                                                                ]
                                                                node[midway,right] {\scriptsize\(\theta_{1}\approx \pgfmathparse{\n2}\pgfmathresult\) rad}
                                                                ;
                                                                \draw[-stealth]
                                                                let
                                                                \p1 =  (O),
                                                                \p2 = (T1),
                                                                \p3 = (T2),
                                                                \p4 = (N),
                                                                \n1 = {atan(-(\x2-\x1)/(\y2-\y1))},
                                                                \n2 = {\n1*3.14159/(180pt)},
                                                                \n3 = {atan(-(\x3-\x1)/(\y3-\y1))},
                                                                \n4 = {\n3*3.14159/(180pt)},
                                                                \n5 = {0.2*(\y4-\y1)},
                                                                \n6 = {0.3*(\y4-\y1)},
                                                                in
                                                                ($(\p1)!0.3!(\p4)$)
                                                                arc[
                                                                        start angle=90,
                                                                        delta angle=\n3,
                                                                radius={\n6},
                                                                ]
                                                                node[midway,above right] {\scriptsize\(\theta_{2}\approx \pgfmathparse{\n4}\pgfmathresult\) rad}
                                                                ;
                                                                \end{tikzpicture}
                                                        </latex-image>
                                                </image>
                                        </figure>
                                </statement>
                        </exercise>
                </page>
        </worksheet>
